1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,200
One eye. One camera.
One microcontroller.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,600
About $64 of parts.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,000
The camera finds a face
and reports where it is.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,400
240 by 240 pixels of eye,
redrawn about 20 times a second.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,800
Two wires carry the face position.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,200
No Pi. No PC. No wifi.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,600
The detection runs on the camera,
not on a computer.

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,000
A second eye costs under $12.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,400
The blinks are not scripted.

10
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,000
It replaced a sensor
that went out of production.

11
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,500
It runs the eyes on my robot face,
IRIS.
